<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>The relationship between social media use, time management, and academic performance among university students.</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.15; margin: 2.54cm; color: #1a1a1a; }
  h1 { font-size: 20pt; } h2 { font-size: 15pt; } h3 { font-size: 12pt; }
  cite { color: #4f46e5; font-style: normal; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 0.5em 0 1em; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #999; padding: 6px 8px; font-size: 10pt; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f0f0f0; font-weight: 700; }
</style></head>
<body><h1>The relationship between social media use, time management, and academic performance among university students.</h1><h2>Abstract</h2><p>This paper synthesizes existing literature to examine the intricate relationship between social media use, time management, and academic performance among university students. The review characterizes prevalent patterns of social media engagement, analyzes its documented effects on time management practices, and evaluates its overall impact on academic outcomes.</p><p>The evidence suggests that while social media offers opportunities for collaborative learning and information sharing, excessive and non-academic use consistently correlates with poor time management, reduced concentration, and lower academic achievement. Conversely, moderate and purposeful academic social media use can positively influence learning. Key themes highlight the importance of digital self-discipline and effective time management as moderators of these impacts. Limitations in the existing literature include a predominant reliance on self-reported data, cross-sectional designs that preclude causal inferences, and a geographical imbalance in studies, with limited representation from the Global South. The synthesis concludes that social media’s influence on academic performance is largely contingent on students' usage patterns rather than the platforms themselves.</p><h2>Introduction</h2><p>University students today navigate a complex academic landscape significantly influenced by pervasive digital technologies, particularly social media platforms <cite data-citation-id="" data-occurrence-id="bb824ea2-ee86-4ce7-a23f-c621299cf6d7" data-items="[{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S1&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;S1&quot;,&quot;canonicalId&quot;:&quot;50c0f715-5ed4-66e3-96d9-0b8fb9aa09d6&quot;,&quot;openAlexWorkId&quot;:&quot;W7168081275&quot;,&quot;pmid&quot;:null,&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;OpenAlex&quot;,&quot;providerRecordId&quot;:&quot;https://openalex.org/W7168081275&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Time Spent on Social Media and its Impact on Academic Performance: Evidence from University Students in Sargodha, Pakistan&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://ojs.pssr.org.pk/journal/article/download/1159/947&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;web&quot;,&quot;passageStart&quot;:null,&quot;passageEnd&quot;:null,&quot;doi&quot;:&quot;10.35484/pssr.2025(9-iv)22&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:&quot;Halema Sadia, Muhammad Hassan Babar, Zunaira Ghaffar&quot;,&quot;authorDetails&quot;:[{&quot;family&quot;:&quot;Sadia&quot;,&quot;given&quot;:&quot;Halema&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Halema Sadia&quot;,&quot;orcid&quot;:&quot;https://orcid.org/0009-0008-4477-3319&quot;,&quot;affiliations&quot;:[&quot;University of Sargodha&quot;]},{&quot;family&quot;:&quot;Babar&quot;,&quot;given&quot;:&quot;Muhammad Hassan&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Muhammad Hassan Babar&quot;,&quot;orcid&quot;:null,&quot;affiliations&quot;:[&quot;University of Lahore&quot;]},{&quot;family&quot;:&quot;Ghaffar&quot;,&quot;given&quot;:&quot;Zunaira&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zunaira Ghaffar&quot;,&quot;orcid&quot;:null,&quot;affiliations&quot;:[&quot;University of Sargodha&quot;]}],&quot;year&quot;:2025,&quot;venue&quot;:&quot;Pakistan Social Sciences Review&quot;,&quot;volume&quot;:&quot;9&quot;,&quot;issue&quot;:&quot;IV&quot;,&quot;pages&quot;:null,&quot;workType&quot;:&quot;article&quot;,&quot;publisher&quot;:null,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;,&quot;yearLabel&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S1&quot;},&quot;originalLabel&quot;:&quot;[S1]&quot;},{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S4&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;S4&quot;,&quot;canonicalId&quot;:&quot;4286b9f9-2462-9531-fc7d-9ff6094dcb6c&quot;,&quot;openAlexWorkId&quot;:&quot;W7164532107&quot;,&quot;pmid&quot;:null,&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;OpenAlex&quot;,&quot;providerRecordId&quot;:&quot;https://openalex.org/W7164532107&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;The Influence of Social Media Usage on Students&#39; Academic Performance and Study Habits&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20669918&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;web&quot;,&quot;passageStart&quot;:null,&quot;passageEnd&quot;:null,&quot;doi&quot;:&quot;10.5281/zenodo.20669918&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:&quot;Saroj Chaudhary&quot;,&quot;authorDetails&quot;:[{&quot;family&quot;:&quot;Chaudhary&quot;,&quot;given&quot;:&quot;Saroj&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Saroj Chaudhary&quot;,&quot;orcid&quot;:null,&quot;affiliations&quot;:[]}],&quot;year&quot;:2026,&quot;venue&quot;:&quot;Zenodo (CERN European Organization for Nuclear Research)&quot;,&quot;volume&quot;:null,&quot;issue&quot;:null,&quot;pages&quot;:null,&quot;workType&quot;:&quot;article&quot;,&quot;publisher&quot;:&quot;European Organization for Nuclear Research&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;,&quot;yearLabel&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S4&quot;},&quot;originalLabel&quot;:&quot;[S4]&quot;},{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S14&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;S14&quot;,&quot;canonicalId&quot;:&quot;92275dfc-7b38-ac80-1b93-82662b86b3af&quot;,&quot;openAlexWorkId&quot;:&quot;W7204948599&quot;,&quot;pmid&quot;:null,&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;OpenAlex&quot;,&quot;providerRecordId&quot;:&quot;https://openalex.org/W7204948599&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Assessment of Social Media Addiction, Academic Stress, and Mental Health among College and University Students&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://doi.org/10.66572/ejimapss.2026.v6.i2.99131&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;web&quot;,&quot;passageStart&quot;:null,&quot;passageEnd&quot;:null,&quot;doi&quot;:&quot;10.66572/ejimapss.2026.v6.i2.99131&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:null,&quot;authorDetails&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:2026,&quot;venue&quot;:&quot;European Journal of Integrative Medicinal and Allied Paramedical Spectrum Studies&quot;,&quot;volume&quot;:&quot;6&quot;,&quot;issue&quot;:&quot;2&quot;,&quot;pages&quot;:null,&quot;workType&quot;:&quot;article&quot;,&quot;publisher&quot;:null,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;,&quot;yearLabel&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S14&quot;},&quot;originalLabel&quot;:&quot;[S14]&quot;}]" data-narrative="false">(Sadia, Babar and Ghaffar, 2025; Chaudhary, 2026; European Journal of Integrative Medicinal and Allied Paramedical Spectrum Studies, 2026)</cite>. These platforms offer diverse functionalities, from entertainment and communication to collaborative learning and information sharing <cite data-citation-id="" data-occurrence-id="77f5eafd-0879-4da0-a59d-6494ad1e5ff4" data-items="[{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S1&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;S1&quot;,&quot;canonicalId&quot;:&quot;50c0f715-5ed4-66e3-96d9-0b8fb9aa09d6&quot;,&quot;openAlexWorkId&quot;:&quot;W7168081275&quot;,&quot;pmid&quot;:null,&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;OpenAlex&quot;,&quot;providerRecordId&quot;:&quot;https://openalex.org/W7168081275&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Time Spent on Social Media and its Impact on Academic Performance: Evidence from University Students in Sargodha, Pakistan&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://ojs.pssr.org.pk/journal/article/download/1159/947&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;web&quot;,&quot;passageStart&quot;:null,&quot;passageEnd&quot;:null,&quot;doi&quot;:&quot;10.35484/pssr.2025(9-iv)22&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:&quot;Halema Sadia, Muhammad Hassan Babar, Zunaira Ghaffar&quot;,&quot;authorDetails&quot;:[{&quot;family&quot;:&quot;Sadia&quot;,&quot;given&quot;:&quot;Halema&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Halema Sadia&quot;,&quot;orcid&quot;:&quot;https://orcid.org/0009-0008-4477-3319&quot;,&quot;affiliations&quot;:[&quot;University of Sargodha&quot;]},{&quot;family&quot;:&quot;Babar&quot;,&quot;given&quot;:&quot;Muhammad Hassan&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Muhammad Hassan Babar&quot;,&quot;orcid&quot;:null,&quot;affiliations&quot;:[&quot;University of Lahore&quot;]},{&quot;family&quot;:&quot;Ghaffar&quot;,&quot;given&quot;:&quot;Zunaira&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Zunaira Ghaffar&quot;,&quot;orcid&quot;:null,&quot;affiliations&quot;:[&quot;University of Sargodha&quot;]}],&quot;year&quot;:2025,&quot;venue&quot;:&quot;Pakistan Social Sciences Review&quot;,&quot;volume&quot;:&quot;9&quot;,&quot;issue&quot;:&quot;IV&quot;,&quot;pages&quot;:null,&quot;workType&quot;:&quot;article&quot;,&quot;publisher&quot;:null,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;,&quot;yearLabel&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S1&quot;},&quot;originalLabel&quot;:&quot;[S1]&quot;},{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S2&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;S2&quot;,&quot;canonicalId&quot;:&quot;28ce1149-4303-2730-e196-a95a7770bb92&quot;,&quot;openAlexWorkId&quot;:&quot;W7160121679&quot;,&quot;pmid&quot;:null,&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;OpenAlex&quot;,&quot;providerRecordId&quot;:&quot;https://openalex.org/W7160121679&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;EFFECTS OF SOCIAL MEDIA ON SCHOOL PERFORMANCE: AN INVESTIGATIVE STUDY OF UNDERGRADUATE STUDENTS IN EDO STATE&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://doi.org/10.54922/ijehss.2026.1251&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;web&quot;,&quot;passageStart&quot;:null,&quot;passageEnd&quot;:null,&quot;doi&quot;:&quot;10.54922/ijehss.2026.1251&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:&quot;OMI UJUANBI, Gloria Omolegho&quot;,&quot;authorDetails&quot;:[{&quot;family&quot;:&quot;OMI UJUANBI&quot;,&quot;given&quot;:null,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;OMI UJUANBI&quot;,&quot;orcid&quot;:null,&quot;affiliations&quot;:[&quot;Ambrose Alli University&quot;]},{&quot;family&quot;:&quot;Omolegho&quot;,&quot;given&quot;:&quot;Gloria&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Gloria Omolegho&quot;,&quot;orcid&quot;:null,&quot;affiliations&quot;:[&quot;Ambrose Alli University&quot;]}],&quot;year&quot;:2026,&quot;venue&quot;:&quot;International Journal of Education Humanities and Social Science&quot;,&quot;volume&quot;:&quot;09&quot;,&quot;issue&quot;:&quot;02&quot;,&quot;pages&quot;:&quot;398-410&quot;,&quot;workType&quot;:&quot;article&quot;,&quot;publisher&quot;:null,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;,&quot;yearLabel&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S2&quot;},&quot;originalLabel&quot;:&quot;[S2]&quot;},{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S4&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;S4&quot;,&quot;canonicalId&quot;:&quot;4286b9f9-2462-9531-fc7d-9ff6094dcb6c&quot;,&quot;openAlexWorkId&quot;:&quot;W7164532107&quot;,&quot;pmid&quot;:null,&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;OpenAlex&quot;,&quot;providerRecordId&quot;:&quot;https://openalex.org/W7164532107&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;The Influence of Social Media Usage on Students&#39; Academic Performance and Study Habits&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20669918&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;web&quot;,&quot;passageStart&quot;:null,&quot;passageEnd&quot;:null,&quot;doi&quot;:&quot;10.5281/zenodo.20669918&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:&quot;Saroj Chaudhary&quot;,&quot;authorDetails&quot;:[{&quot;family&quot;:&quot;Chaudhary&quot;,&quot;given&quot;:&quot;Saroj&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Saroj Chaudhary&quot;,&quot;orcid&quot;:null,&quot;affiliations&quot;:[]}],&quot;year&quot;:2026,&quot;venue&quot;:&quot;Zenodo (CERN European Organization for Nuclear Research)&quot;,&quot;volume&quot;:null,&quot;issue&quot;:null,&quot;pages&quot;:null,&quot;workType&quot;:&quot;article&quot;,&quot;publisher&quot;:&quot;European Organization for Nuclear Research&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;,&quot;yearLabel&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S4&quot;},&quot;originalLabel&quot;:&quot;[S4]&quot;},{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S14&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;S14&quot;,&quot;canonicalId&quot;:&quot;92275dfc-7b38-ac80-1b93-82662b86b3af&quot;,&quot;openAlexWorkId&quot;:&quot;W7204948599&quot;,&quot;pmid&quot;:null,&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;OpenAlex&quot;,&quot;providerRecordId&quot;:&quot;https://openalex.org/W7204948599&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Assessment of Social Media Addiction, Academic Stress, and Mental Health among College and University Students&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://doi.org/10.66572/ejimapss.2026.v6.i2.99131&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;web&quot;,&quot;passageStart&quot;:null,&quot;passageEnd&quot;:null,&quot;doi&quot;:&quot;10.66572/ejimapss.2026.v6.i2.99131&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:null,&quot;authorDetails&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:2026,&quot;venue&quot;:&quot;European Journal of Integrative Medicinal and Allied Paramedical Spectrum Studies&quot;,&quot;volume&quot;:&quot;6&quot;,&quot;issue&quot;:&quot;2&quot;,&quot;pages&quot;:null,&quot;workType&quot;:&quot;article&quot;,&quot;publisher&quot;:null,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;,&quot;yearLabel&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S14&quot;},&quot;originalLabel&quot;:&quot;[S14]&quot;}]" data-narrative="false">(Sadia, Babar and Ghaffar, 2025; Chaudhary, 2026; OMI UJUANBI and Omolegho, 2026; European Journal of Integrative Medicinal and Allied Paramedical Spectrum Studies, 2026)</cite>. While social media presents opportunities for enhanced peer-to-peer interaction and access to educational resources <cite data-citation-id="" data-occurrence-id="d81371bb-d0e8-4a28-b84b-9fa3aa9e2358" data-items="[{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S2&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;S2&quot;,&quot;canonicalId&quot;:&quot;28ce1149-4303-2730-e196-a95a7770bb92&quot;,&quot;openAlexWorkId&quot;:&quot;W7160121679&quot;,&quot;pmid&quot;:null,&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;OpenAlex&quot;,&quot;providerRecordId&quot;:&quot;https://openalex.org/W7160121679&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;EFFECTS OF SOCIAL MEDIA ON SCHOOL PERFORMANCE: AN INVESTIGATIVE STUDY OF UNDERGRADUATE STUDENTS IN EDO STATE&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://doi.org/10.54922/ijehss.2026.1251&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;web&quot;,&quot;passageStart&quot;:null,&quot;passageEnd&quot;:null,&quot;doi&quot;:&quot;10.54922/ijehss.2026.1251&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:&quot;OMI UJUANBI, Gloria Omolegho&quot;,&quot;authorDetails&quot;:[{&quot;family&quot;:&quot;OMI UJUANBI&quot;,&quot;given&quot;:null,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;OMI UJUANBI&quot;,&quot;orcid&quot;:null,&quot;affiliations&quot;:[&quot;Ambrose Alli University&quot;]},{&quot;family&quot;:&quot;Omolegho&quot;,&quot;given&quot;:&quot;Gloria&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Gloria Omolegho&quot;,&quot;orcid&quot;:null,&quot;affiliations&quot;:[&quot;Ambrose Alli University&quot;]}],&quot;year&quot;:2026,&quot;venue&quot;:&quot;International Journal of Education Humanities and Social Science&quot;,&quot;volume&quot;:&quot;09&quot;,&quot;issue&quot;:&quot;02&quot;,&quot;pages&quot;:&quot;398-410&quot;,&quot;workType&quot;:&quot;article&quot;,&quot;publisher&quot;:null,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;,&quot;yearLabel&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S2&quot;},&quot;originalLabel&quot;:&quot;[S2]&quot;},{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S3&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;S3&quot;,&quot;canonicalId&quot;:&quot;b61186cc-2965-3b5d-70e0-de17b70d7e2d&quot;,&quot;openAlexWorkId&quot;:&quot;W7129271745&quot;,&quot;pmid&quot;:null,&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;OpenAlex&quot;,&quot;providerRecordId&quot;:&quot;https://openalex.org/W7129271745&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Productive and Problematic Social Media Use and Students’ Academic Outcomes: Mediation by Parent/Teacher Support and Moderation by Time Management Skills (Evidence from Higher Education Institutions in Punjab and Kh