10.66572/ejimapss.2026.v6.i2.99131&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;web&quot;,&quot;passageStart&quot;:null,&quot;passageEnd&quot;:null,&quot;doi&quot;:&quot;10.66572/ejimapss.2026.v6.i2.99131&quot;,&quot;authors&quot;:null,&quot;authorDetails&quot;:[],&quot;year&quot;:2026,&quot;venue&quot;:&quot;European Journal of Integrative Medicinal and Allied Paramedical Spectrum Studies&quot;,&quot;volume&quot;:&quot;6&quot;,&quot;issue&quot;:&quot;2&quot;,&quot;pages&quot;:null,&quot;workType&quot;:&quot;article&quot;,&quot;publisher&quot;:null,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;,&quot;yearLabel&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S14&quot;},&quot;originalLabel&quot;:&quot;[S14]&quot;}]" data-narrative="false">(Sadia, Babar and Ghaffar, 2025; Chaudhary, 2026; OMI UJUANBI and Omolegho, 2026; European Journal of Integrative Medicinal and Allied Paramedical Spectrum Studies, 2026)</cite>. WhatsApp, Facebook, and YouTube are consistently identified as popular platforms <cite data-citation-id="" data-occurrence-id="19ae24e7-c9ad-4741-95b1-8fb9c1383f42" data-items="[{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;fb7822bf-c876-49f5-9489-213f495ab409:S7&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:{&quot;sourceId&quot;:&quot;S7&quot;,&quot;canonicalId&quot;:&quot;8fb42fd7-cbdd-db81-7b9b-ca7b33d000fb&quot;,&quot;openAlexWorkId&quot;:&quot;W7215165637&quot;,&quot;pmid&quot;:null,&quot;provider&quot;:&quot;OpenAlex&quot;,&quot;providerRecordId&quot;:&quot;https://openalex.org/W7215165637&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;INFLUENCE OF SOCIAL MEDIA PLATFORM USE ON ACADEMIC PERFORMANCE OF COOPERATIVE ECONOMICS AND MANAGEMENT STUDENTS AT NNAMDI AZIKIWE UNIVERSITY, AWKA&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://ijmsspcs.com/index.php/IJMSSPCS/article/download/870/943&quot;,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;web&quot;,&quot;passageStart&quot;:null,&quot;passageEnd&quot;:null,&quot;doi&quot;:null,&quot;authors&quot;:&quot;Lovelyn Chinwendu Ajubiga, Obianuju Chekwube-Aziekwe, Chinyere Chigozie Akpunonu, Stephanie Chidio